	<entry name="ShadowWeaver" value="Shadow weaver"/>
	<entry name="ShadowWeaverFlavor" value="Among the Warp Spiders of the Aeldari, there is an old tale of a shrine warrior known as Dy'bree. During a catastrophic passage through the hidden strands of the Webway, he glimpsed something that no mortal mind was meant to witness. Though he returned alive, he never spoke another word. Instead, he forged a unique weapon — Shadow Weaver, binding fragments of that terrible vision into its psycho-reactive core.
When Shadow Weaver unleashes its payload, it does more than cast monofilament death across the battlefield. For a fleeting instant, reality itself grows thin. Darkness gathers where the weapon strikes, and shadows twist into impossible shapes. Those caught within its reach often report hearing distant whispers moments before they perish, as if something beyond the veil has become aware of them.
To the Aeldari, the weapon stands as a warning of the price of forbidden knowledge. To their enemies, it is merely the herald of a silent and inescapable end.

«You fear the darkness. Dy'bree and his Warp Spiders walk where it was born.»"/>
